Statement of modifications (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------------

The following files are derived from Codex Security and carry modifications:

  plugin/skills/**/SKILL.md
      Rebranded to Claude Code skill invocation syntax and environment variable
      names. The three top-level scan workflows (security-scan,
      security-diff-scan, deep-security-scan) additionally had their setup,
      completion, and orchestration sections rewritten: the Codex desktop MCP
      app surface they described has no Claude Code equivalent, and scan
      registration, sealing, and reporting moved into the CLI.

  plugin/references/config-preflight.md
  plugin/preflight/capability-profiles.toml
  plugin/scripts/config_preflight.py
      Rewritten. The originals discovered and layered Codex `config.toml` files
      to evaluate sandbox mode, approval policy, and native multi-agent v2.
      Claude Code exposes none of those as user configuration, so these now
      evaluate capabilities a session can actually observe about its own tool
      surface.

  plugin/references/final-report.md
      The "Codex Review Directives" section, which emitted `::code-comment{...}`
      directives for Codex app rendering, was replaced with a plain final-response
      contract. Completion guidance was updated: the CLI owns sealing.

  plugin/references/*.md, plugin/skills/**/*.md
      Product naming, skill invocation syntax, and environment variable names
      rebranded. Analytical content (validation guidance, severity policy,
      attack-path rules, repository-wide scan procedure) is unmodified.

  plugin/scripts/workbench_db.py
      Plugin manifest path changed from `.codex-plugin/plugin.json` to
      `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`. Error text rebranded.

  plugin/scripts/finalize_scan_contract.py
      PRODUCER_NAME changed to "claude-security-plugin"; SARIF tool driver name
      changed to "Claude Security". Contract logic unmodified.

  plugin/scripts/*.py
      Docstrings and error messages rebranded. Logic otherwise unmodified.

  plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json
      Replaces the upstream `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`.

The on-disk scan contract identifiers are deliberately UNCHANGED, so scan
bundles remain interchangeable with upstream tooling:

  documentType: "codex-security.scan-manifest"
  documentType: "codex-security.findings"
  documentType: "codex-security.coverage"
  fingerprints.algorithm: "codex-security/v1"


Removed
-------

  mcp/                    The Codex MCP app server, which embedded the Codex SDK
                          and spawned `codex exec` workers.
  .app.json               Codex app connector registration.
  skills/*/agents/openai.yaml
                          Codex-only skill interface metadata.

The following upstream capabilities are not ported: containerized bulk scans,
the `bulk-scan` and `install-hook` subcommands, and deep-scan resume.


